comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T13:16:57.715Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing: semantic search for 'DeepScan CodeFactor analyze direct pushes to main so direct commits carry exact analyzer evidence' returned only closed lineage (pm-39cqqx, pm-xcrlkl, pm-u1baah, pm-ji5c, pm-izid) and no open owner; pm-e70zh5 owns the rate, pm-44u3wt the cron window, pm-uenmu9 the same-day guard, pm-k9m6wc release immutability. Evidence: gh api commits/5da0aa6e5/status lists codecov/patch only and check-runs list nothing from an analyzer; commits/41ac9470f/status lists DeepScan, CodeRabbit, Hound and check-runs list codefactor-io/CodeFactor and semgrep. Scheduled run 34199116643 failed step 'Verify release analyzer provenance before build' with direct_main_policy refuse_without_exact_commit_analyzer_evidence."
  "2026-09-12T21:09:35.765Z","harness:codex","Live recurrence 2026-09-12: main CI run 34717518299 failed only Release analyzer readiness on 1e60ce072d9af3e819ed58bf0ec2100bf45dad40. This head arrived directly on main and lacks exact-commit or reviewed identical-tree analyzer evidence. The connected telemetry PR must restore analyzed provenance without weakening the gate. GitHub open PR and all three security alert inventories were empty."
